        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila willistoni subcellular Turing wavelength (1.5 µm, 0 Ma) (Drosophila willistoni)",
        "Drosophila willistoni subcellular Turing wavelength (1.5 µm, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila willistoni morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila willistoni specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila willistoni" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim Clark 2007 measured a 1.5 µm Turing wavelength.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim D. virilis is a literal ancestor or D. yakuba a literal descendant.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim sex-comb loss is produced by this reaction-diffusion system.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not reuse slot 2931 parameters (86 µm, alpha_scale 1.63, beta_offset 0.38).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Allometry λ ∝ L_body^0.35 and a cell diameter linear in body length are slot-specific reconstructions.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The periodic patch stands in for the repeating granule lattice inside an epidermal cell.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: a=0.072, b=1.186, gamma=0.84, Du=0.015919 µm², Dv=0.214909 µm² are chosen so λ_max=1.466 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Clark et al. 2007 describe the D. willistoni genome, sex-comb loss, and inversion polymorphism.",
        "reported_in_source: Hanson 2019 is a CC BY-SA 4.0 photograph of an adult D. willistoni female.",
        "reported_in_source: Jeong et al. 2008 and Wittkopp et al. 2009 describe Drosophila abdominal pigmentation divergence relevant to the yakuba successor and the virilis-group predecessor.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 gives the two-species kinetics used here.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 gives the diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: The photograph resolves the whole fly. The 1.5 µm field is painted onto the segmented abdomen; it is not a micrograph of granules." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila willistoni (Neotropical Rainforest Sophophora Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
